WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.720
A running track, seen from above.

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:06.600
Two straights, joined by
two semicircular bends.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.780
The runners crouch at the start.

4
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.550
But the start line isn't straight across.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.420
Every outer lane begins further ahead.

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.960
Is that a head start
for the outside lanes?

7
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.970
Or is something else going on?

8
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.620
In this mission, you'll find the
perimeter of a composite shape,

9
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.860
like a rectangle with a
semicircle on each end.

10
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.950
You'll use the circumference of a circle,

11
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.580
two pi r, and its area, pi r squared.

12
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:36.130
And you'll find areas of triangles,
parallelograms and trapezia.

13
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.910
Your mission: explain why runners in
the outer lanes start further ahead.
